<%# Deliberately empty. Overrides
    spree_admin-5.6.1/app/views/spree/admin/shared/sidebar/_enterprise_edition_notice.html.erb

    That partial is an upsell: it renders for anyone who can manage the store while
    SpreeEnterprise is not defined, and links to spreecommerce.org/pricing. The client
    asked for it gone — "Can you block the Enterprise notice from showing?" — and this is
    his shop, on his server, shown to his staff.

    An empty override rather than dismissing it, because dismissal is stored in the SESSION
    (session[:spree_enterprise_edition_notice_dismissed]), so it returns for every new
    sign-in and on every other browser.

    A view override is last in the order of preference in CLAUDE.md, and here there is no
    hook to use instead. The usual cost of an override is going stale against the gem, and
    an empty file cannot: there is nothing in it to fall behind.
%>
